   102	## 3. Per-component geometry and numerical identities
   103	
   104	The only stated generic-fibre identity that is componentwise is
   105	\(a_i+W_i=N\).  It gives
   106	\[
   107	 (a_A,W_A)=(3,2),\qquad (a_B,W_B)=(4,1).
   108	\]
   109	The correction/cover floor gives \(K_A=1,K_B=0\).  The aggregate identity is
   110	therefore
   111	\[
   112	 W_A+W_B+K_{\rm tot}=2+1+1=4=N-1. \tag{3.1}
   113	\]
