   117	A particularly tempting but invalid kill is to apply the irreducible formula
   118	\(K=a-1\) separately to \(D_A\), obtaining \(1\ne3-1\).  The Euler
   119	stratification is global and does not split this way.  Combining (3.1) with
   120	\(a_A=5-W_A\) instead gives the correct relation
   121	\[
   122	 K_{\rm tot}=a_A-1-W_B=3-1-1=1. \tag{3.2}
   123	\]
   124	The other component's weight is exactly the apparently missing unit.  Moving
   125	immersivity from \(D_B\) to \(D_A\), or moving the irreducible Euler identity
   126	in the same way, would repeat the component-carrier error highlighted in the
   127	charge.
