   192	\((r,\delta,\mu_{\rm Milnor})=(1,1,2)\).  More generally
   193	\(\mu_{\rm Milnor}=2\delta-r+1\); S1a has \(r-1=0\) but
   194	\(\delta\ge1\), while S1b has \(r-1=1\) but \(\delta\ge3\).  Thus the
   195	\(N=4\) one-node exclusion pattern cannot be transferred by replacing a node
   196	with a cusp.  The charged covering stratification contains neither a Milnor
   197	number nor a vanishing-cycle term.
