   222	## 5. \(S_5\)-monodromy and representation constraints
   223	
   224	Let \(\rho\) be the five-sheet monodromy.  It is transitive; \(D_B\)-meridians
   225	map to the identity, so \(\rho\) factors through
   226	\(\pi_1(\mathbb C^2-D_A)\).  Every \(D_A\)-meridian is a transposition.  A
   227	transitive subgroup generated by transpositions is the full symmetric group
   228	(the transposition-support graph is connected), hence
   229	\[
   230	 \rho:\pi_1(\mathbb C^2-D_A)\twoheadrightarrow S_5. \tag{5.1}
   231	\]
