   463	| **P3a/P3b** `(2,0)+(1,0)+(1,0)` | survives all gates | **SURVIVOR S2** |
   464	| S2 rows with `M_∞ + 2T ≤ 3d − 3` | Gate N-A-RES `[P]` | KILLED row-by-row |
   465	
   466	## 5. Survivors, fully typed (the N=5 residual cage)
   467	
   468	Two configurations survive every gate. Both have the same shape: **one branched
   469	component `D_br` with `(W, a) = (2, 3)` and meridian a transposition, plus one
   470	or two unbranched polynomial-curve components carrying the trivial
   471	dicritical(s).** They differ only in whether the branched component carries a
   472	correction.
   473	
   474	### 5.1 Survivor S1 (from P1) — the cuspidal cage
   475	
   476	| item | value |
   477	|---|---|
   478	| dicriticals | `l_A = (mu, corr, s) = (2, 1, 1)` over `D_A`; `l_B = (1, 0, 1)` over `D_B` |
   479	| components | `m = 2`; `(W_A, a_A) = (2, 3)`, `(W_B, a_B) = (1, 4)` |
   480	| corrections | `K_tot = 1`, all of it at one parameter `t_0 ∈ l'_A` |
   481	| meridians | `gamma_A` of type `1^3 2`; `gamma_B` trivial |
   482	| `D_A` | polynomial curve, `D~_A ≃ A^1`, one place at infinity, birationally parametrized; `eta_A` critical at exactly one parameter `t_0` |
   483	| the special point | `p_0 = eta_A(t_0)`, `M_{t_0} = e·mu + k = 2 + 1 = 3`; the branch at `p_0` is **singular** |
   484	| other singularities of `D_A` | double points of two smooth branches only (`r ≤ 2` by (LOC-1)), each with `a_p = 1` |
   485	| `D_B` | polynomial curve, `eta_B` immersive, all branches smooth, `a_p = 5 − r_{B,p}` off `D_A` |
   486	| degree | `deg D_A = 3 + 2g + Σ_∞ ≥ 4` (Gate TG); `deg D_B ≥ 1` |
   487	
   488	Sub-cases at `p_0`, from (LOC) with `K_{p_0} = 1`:
   489	
   490	- **S1a** `r_{A,p_0} = 1` (unibranch cusp): `a_{p_0} = 2` if `p_0 ∉ D_B`, and
   491	  `a_{p_0} = 2 − r_{B,p_0}` if `p_0 ∈ D_B`. In both cases Lemma C gives
   492	  `#Fix(G_{p_0}) = 2` exactly.
   493	- **S1b** `r_{A,p_0} = 2` (the singular branch shares `p_0` with a smooth
   494	  branch of `D_A`): `a_{p_0} = 0`, `#Fix(G_{p_0}) = 0`, cluster sizes `3 + 2`.
   495	
   496	**Why this is genuinely new relative to `N = 4`.** The `N = 4` residual
   497	(C19 §1, ALLN §5.2) had `corr = 0` on both dicriticals, so its branched
   498	component had only double points of smooth branches. At `N = 5` the budget is
   499	one unit larger and P1 spends it on a correction, which — because Lemma B
   500	forbids a ramified cover here — is forced onto `d eta_A`. So **S1 is a
   501	cuspidal-curve residual with no `N = 4` analogue**, and it sits *outside* the
   502	hypothesis class of the promoted Theorem N-A / Corollary N-A-RES, which require
   503	every singularity to be a double point of two smooth branches. No promoted gate
   504	reaches S1.
   505	
   506	### 5.2 Survivor S2 (from P3a/P3b) — the PI1-S5 cage
   507	
