   537	Chau `[L]` (Theorem 1, Corollary 2, arXiv:math/0305088 pp. 1–2) adds two
   538	structure pins that hold for both survivors and have no analogue in the charged
   539	inputs: (i) every component of `A_F` is parametrized as
   540	`ξ ↦ (A ξ^{m_i d} + …, B ξ^{m_i e} + …)` with one fixed coprime pair `(d, e)`
   541	independent of the component, so all component degrees are multiples of a common
   542	`max(d, e)` and the ratio `deg p_i / deg q_i` is the same for every component;
   543	(ii) `A_F` has **one point at infinity** — the branched component and every
   544	unbranched component meet `L_∞` at the *same* point, each with a single place
   545	there, with Newton–Puiseux `u = c v^{d/e} + …`. So the reducible cage is not
   546	"several unrelated curves": it is a bouquet of polynomial curves, pairwise
   547	tangent to one common direction at one common point of `L_∞`, of which exactly
   548	one is branched.
